  "response_text": "The stack allocation method we used works by initially setting a maximum amount of stack memory, 0x4000 (or 16 KB), starting at that memory value, and working downwards in memory values. MSP_init_val is an initially large number. By subtracting 0x400 from the address of MSP_inti_val, we can calculate a new address to have PSP_val point to. This offset of the initial MSP and PSP values is done so that there are no memory overlaps between MSP and PSP. We need to know the initial location of MSP for this to work since the allocation of PSP_val is dependent on the initial value of MSP.\\n",
